---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GuideArticle from '../../components/v2/templates/GuideArticle.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../../data/images';
import { getPageSEO } from '../../utils/seo';

const faqItems = [
  { question: 'Where should I begin with an order?', answer: 'Read the current order information first, then follow the restaurant workflow through ingredients, cooking, food, and serving.' },
  { question: 'Where can I review ingredient information?', answer: 'Use the Ingredients Hub for the directory and individual ingredient entries.' },
  { question: 'Where can I review cooking equipment?', answer: 'Use the Equipment Hub and Stoves Directory for cooking-equipment pages.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout pageId="guides-cooking-and-serving" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }, { label: getPageSEO('guides-cooking-and-serving').h1 }]}>
<GuideArticle
  title={getPageSEO('guides-cooking-and-serving').h1}
  kicker="Kitchen workflow guide"
  intro="Read the customer request, follow the current cooking prompts, and deliver the completed food to the intended customer."
  tableOfContents
  heroImage={siteImages.foodHero}
  previousPage={{ label: 'Co-op Guide', href: '/guides/co-op-guide/' }}
  nextPage={{ label: 'How to Hire Workers', href: '/guides/how-to-hire-workers/' }}
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Recipes', href: '/recipes/', description: 'Learn how Recipes connect ingredients, cooking, and food.' },
    { label: 'Ingredients', href: '/ingredients/', description: 'Browse the Ingredient directory and entity pages.' },
    { label: 'Equipment', href: '/equipment/', description: 'Explore cooking equipment and restaurant tools.' },
    { label: 'Food', href: '/food/', description: 'Review how prepared food connects with restaurant service.' },
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="direct-answer">Direct Answer</h2>
  <p>Use the current customer and order prompts, move the request into the kitchen workflow, wait for the game to show that the food is ready, and serve it to the intended customer. Exact recipe inputs and equipment performance belong on separately verified pages.</p>

  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>This guide explains the general restaurant flow. Recipes, Ingredients, Food, and Equipment remain separate Wiki sections so each topic can be explored without placing unsupported details into one article.</p>

  <h2 id="how-it-works">How It Works</h2>
  <p>Public gameplay consistently shows a customer-to-kitchen-to-service loop. The Wiki summarizes it in five stages:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Order:</strong> read the information currently shown for the customer.</li>
    <li><strong>Ingredients:</strong> consult the ingredient information required by the current interface.</li>
    <li><strong>Cooking:</strong> follow the live kitchen and equipment prompts.</li>
    <li><strong>Food:</strong> keep the prepared item associated with the current service task.</li>
    <li><strong>Serving:</strong> return to the dining area and complete the customer interaction.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="cooking-and-serving-process">Cooking and Serving Process</h2>
  <h3 id="read-the-order">Read the Order</h3>
  <p>Pause long enough to understand the current request before moving into preparation. When several tasks are visible, keep each one clearly associated with the correct customer.</p>
  <h3 id="prepare-the-kitchen">Prepare the Kitchen</h3>
  <p>Review Ingredients and Equipment information, then keep the active kitchen task easy to identify. Organize the work area so prepared food is not confused with another task.</p>
  <h3 id="complete-service">Complete Service</h3>
  <p>Move from the kitchen back to the dining area and finish the current customer interaction before taking on more work than the team can follow.</p>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Read the current order information before beginning preparation.</li>
    <li>Keep ingredients, cooking equipment, and prepared food visually organized.</li>
    <li>Use clear handoffs when playing with teammates.</li>
    <li>Finish visible tasks before adding more restaurant work.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="common-mistakes">Common Issues</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Starting preparation before reading the current order.</li>
    <li>Losing track of which prepared food belongs with the active task.</li>
    <li>Leaving the kitchen and dining route difficult to follow.</li>
    <li>Having multiple players repeat the same task while another area waits.</li>
  </ul>

  <FAQ slot="faq" items={faqItems} />
</GuideArticle>
</BaseLayout>
